repository-code: "https://github.com/Sulla-Soglia/palimpseste"
abstract: >-
  A building is a palimpsest: each occupation scraped the surface and wrote a
  new layer, and the old layers show through. Alsace-Lorraine changed hands
  between France and Germany five times. This project asks whether a
  convolutional network trained on building facades can detect those strata,
  and whether its attention maps decompose a facade into cultural-temporal
  layers — the architectural counterpart of training stratigraphy in AI
  systems.
keywords:
  - deep learning
  - cultural heritage
  - computer vision
  - digital humanities
  - explainable AI
